PROGRAMMING 

DATA TYPES
  Integer     whole numbers          int / integer     42
  Float       decimals               float / double    3.14
  Boolean     true or false          bool              true / false
  Character   single symbol          char              'A'
  String      text                   str / string      "hello"
  Array/List  ordered collection     [] / list         [1, 2, 3]
  Object/Map  key-value pairs        dict / object     {"a": 1}

VARIABLES
  Declare     type name;
  Assign      name = value;
  Init        type name = value;
  Naming      letters, digits, _     start with letter or _
  Scope       local (inside block)   global (outside)
  Constants   cannot be changed      const / final / ALL_CAPS

OPERATORS
  Arithmetic  +  -  *  /  %  **
  Comparison  ==  !=  <  >  <=  >=
  Logical     &&  ||  !     and or not
  Assignment  =  +=  -=  *=  /=

CONTROL FLOW
  if / else if / else
  for         counted loop
  while       condition loop
  switch      multi-way branch
  break       exit loop / switch
  continue    skip to next iteration

FUNCTIONS
  Define      returnType name(params) { body }
  Call        name(arguments)
  Return      send value back
  Parameters  inputs to the function

I/O & BASICS
  Output      print / cout / console.log
  Input       read / cin / input()
  Comments    // line     /* block */
  Errors      syntax, runtime, logic
